{"schema":1,"fm":{"schema":1,"id":"build-event-volunteer-rota","kind":"prompt","title":"Build an event volunteer rota","description":"Builds a shift rota for event volunteers or staff from roles and availability, with coverage per area, breaks, briefings, leads, buffers for no-shows and a message telling each person where to be.","category":"event-planning","version":"1.0.0","status":"incubating","stage":["plan","operate"],"role":["individual","operations-manager"],"requires":["none"],"inputs":["text","dataset"],"output":["table","message"],"risk":"read-only","invocation":"user","effort":"standard","interaction":"one-shot","model_tier":"frontier","reasoning":"recommended","level":"beginner","depth":"specific","tags":["volunteer-rota","shift-planning","event-staffing","stewards","coverage"],"pairs_with":{"prompts":["write-run-of-show","recruit-volunteers","plan-event-check-in"]},"args":[{"name":"roles","description":"The roles or areas and how many people each needs at what times, for example \"entrance: 3 from 9 to 17\", \"bar: 2 from 12 to 22\", and any roles needing training or checks (first aid, cash, children).","type":"text","required":true},{"name":"people","description":"Volunteers or staff with their availability, skills and any limits (under 18, can't lift, wants to work with a friend). A pasted list is fine.","type":"text","required":true}],"output_contract":{"format":"markdown","sections":["Coverage check","Rota","Qualified roles","Briefing","No-show plan","Message to volunteers"]},"authorship":"ai-assisted","authors":["gabrielanhaia"],"last_reviewed":"2026-10-11","changelog":[{"version":"1.0.0","note":"First version."}]},"body":"<context>\nYou schedule event volunteers. You know: shifts longer than four hours without a break burn people out; breaks need cover so posts are never empty; around 10 to 20 percent of volunteers do not turn up, so key posts need a reserve; each area needs a named lead; roles involving cash, children, alcohol service or first aid may need checks, training or age limits; volunteers stay when they get a clear briefing, food and thanks; and a rota is only useful if each person gets a short message telling them where and when.\n\nRoles: {{roles}}\nPeople: {{people}}\n</context>\n\n<task>\n1. Coverage check: total person-hours needed versus available, by time block; show any gap and suggest fixes (shorter shifts, fewer posts at quiet times, recruiting more).\n2. Build the rota: time blocks of three to four hours, people assigned to roles, breaks with cover, leads per area, and reserves.\n3. Respect each person's limits and skills; put trained or checked people on roles that need them, and flag any role where nobody qualifies.\n4. Briefing: when and where volunteers meet, and what the lead covers.\n5. A no-show plan: who to call, which posts to leave empty first.\n6. A short template message to each volunteer with their shift, role, meeting point and contact.\n</task>\n\n<constraints>\n- Use only the people given; never invent names. Use [unfilled] for gaps.\n- Do not place under-18s or untrained people in roles that need training or checks.\n- Show the person-hours arithmetic.\n</constraints>\n\n<output_format>\n## Coverage check\n## Rota\nA table: Time | Role or area | Person | Lead.\n## Qualified roles\n## Briefing\n## No-show plan\n## Message to volunteers\n</output_format>","steps":[]}
